WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.492 --> 00:00:08.145
The task of making order,
victorious over chaos or randomness.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:14.434
If you take this seriously,
you will look upon it as warfare.

00:00:15.577 --> 00:00:19.903
Alan Watts was a 20th century British
American philosopher born in 1915.

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:23.260
He is renowned for his wit,
eloquence and success in translating

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:26.235
and infusing Eastern philosophy
into Western world.

00:00:26.487 --> 00:00:29.473
Watts is regarded as being greatly
responsible for the popularization

00:00:29.679 --> 00:00:33.523
of Buddhist and Zen principles in the West,
inspiring the beat and hippie movements

00:00:33.673 --> 00:00:37.675
in the United States during the 60s and 70s
and causing major cultural shifts away

00:00:37.675 --> 00:00:39.565
from traditional western values.

00:00:39.775 --> 00:00:44.695
During his life before dying in 1973,
at 58 Watts published over 25 books

00:00:44.695 --> 00:00:47.728
and articles on various
Western and Eastern theories

00:00:47.894 --> 00:00:50.365
and was the first to write a best-selling
book on Buddhism entitled

00:00:50.495 --> 00:00:53.105
The way of Zen published in 1957.

00:00:53.305 --> 00:00:56.889
Watts's unique ability to understand,
conceive and translate complex

00:00:57.086 --> 00:01:00.460
alternative philosophies into practical
digestible language.

00:01:00.665 --> 00:01:04.390
Makes it clear why he is one of the most
enjoyed and influential philosophers

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:06.057
in recent history.

00:01:06.189 --> 00:01:09.590
Watts's interest in Eastern philosophy
stem from his childhood enjoyment

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:13.519
of Chinese and Japanese storybooks,
as well as his affinity with Eastern aesthetic.

00:01:13.663 --> 00:01:16.127
He found that things like
light, colour and nature

00:01:16.307 --> 00:01:19.467
were shown in profoundly beautiful
and provoking ways within Eastern art

00:01:19.637 --> 00:01:22.029
and he wondered what it was
that allowed these artists to see

00:01:22.236 --> 00:01:24.346
and consider the world with such lucidity.

00:01:24.511 --> 00:01:28.318
Watts was born in what is now South-East
London and was initially raised Christian.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.756
However during Watts's
developing younger years

00:01:30.893 --> 00:01:34.566
he began to find that Christianity's methods
of understanding and dealing with life

00:01:34.736 --> 00:01:39.116
left him unappeased unfulfilled and often
with more problems than solutions.

00:01:39.285 --> 00:01:43.437
In Watts's mind Christianity did not attempt
in any real sense to answer things like

00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:45.928
what the true nature of the universe is,
what the self is,

00:01:46.088 --> 00:01:48.506
what the meaning of life is
and how to deal with it all.

00:01:48.676 --> 00:01:52.359
Rather Christianity appeared more interested
in studying and maintaining history

00:01:52.519 --> 00:01:56.686
and remained and firmly transfixed on the idea
that there is some tyrannical like God figure

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.142
controlling everything.

00:01:58.332 --> 00:02:01.752
This idea of an authority figure controlling
the universe was both unappealing

00:02:01.912 --> 00:02:03.261
and insensible to Watts.

00:02:03.391 --> 00:02:07.441
And so in combination with his growing fondness
and curiosity with the eastern aesthetic

00:02:07.621 --> 00:02:09.834
he would embark on his journey in to Buddhism.

00:02:10.006 --> 00:02:12.688
What drew Watts further into Buddhism
was that in Buddhism

00:02:12.838 --> 00:02:17.058
rather than a tyrannical like god controlling
everything with some rational or moral intension.

00:02:17.218 --> 00:02:18.975
There is a universal consciousness,

00:02:19.102 --> 00:02:22.496
which everything is an interconnected
and interdependent part of

00:02:22.626 --> 00:02:26.335
a singular essence to life that follows
its own nature with no boss.

00:02:26.465 --> 00:02:30.528
Every object and every person is merely
an expression of this universal nature

00:02:30.813 --> 00:02:33.396
following the nature of itself
for the mere sake of itself.

00:02:33.598 --> 00:02:36.922
Watts found this concept to be far more
reasonable, human and useful

00:02:37.097 --> 00:02:38.328
to the experience of life.

00:02:38.478 --> 00:02:41.882
As Watts study, consider and practice
Eastern ideas like this one,

00:02:42.062 --> 00:02:44.749
he found that he experienced
a certain bliss in their realization,

00:02:44.921 --> 00:02:47.736
often regarded as
enlightenment or awakening.

00:02:47.906 --> 00:02:51.452
Life became richer, anxieties and
fears reduced if not disappeared

00:02:51.651 --> 00:02:54.007
and peace and connection
with nature blossomed.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.647
It was this that Watts wanted
to share with the Westener,

00:02:56.838 --> 00:03:02.136
- an individual whom Watts felt deeply needed
a way out or in, depending on where he stood.

00:03:02.332 --> 00:03:05.196
With the distinctively diverse background
in understanding of both

00:03:05.415 --> 00:03:08.224
Western and Eastern worlds
from a cultural standpoint,

00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:13.018
Watts found that much of the western world
was intensely alienated and conflicted.

00:03:13.218 --> 00:03:17.821
Often obsessed with status, wealth, consumption
and success in being right or the best.

00:03:18.045 --> 00:03:21.097
Yet even when one successful in the
Western ideal of success,

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.909
they still appeared to remain lost and
disconnected from themselves,

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.116
their fellow human and nature itself.

00:03:26.301 --> 00:03:30.078
The idea that a successful business,
a new luxury product sold or bought

00:03:30.259 --> 00:03:33.677
a higher status, a social power
or anything alike could resolve

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:37.396
the human experience of isolation,
anxiety and vulnerability

00:03:37.596 --> 00:03:39.416
was exceptionally foolish in Watts's mind.

00:03:39.616 --> 00:03:43.650
Furthermore it appeared that the Western
religious idea of an absolute morality

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:47.759
and authoritative God did not really assist
the westerner and his or her ability

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:51.721
to resolve these behaviours or help any
spiritual essence in themselves.

00:03:51.938 --> 00:03:54.936
Rather it only further detach them from
the physical of metaphysical world,

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.430
by making them a subject of everything
instead of a part of everything.

00:03:58.653 --> 00:04:02.638
The principles of Zen and Watts's teaching
diverged through others significantly.

00:04:02.821 --> 00:04:05.201
As humans we have
a very peculiar consciousness

00:04:05.375 --> 00:04:09.218
that is aware of what it is perceiving and
furthermore identifies with its awareness.

00:04:09.431 --> 00:04:14.222
This self-identification is generally
regarded as ego and as a result of our ego

00:04:14.388 --> 00:04:17.178
we tend to feel as though we are detached
from what we are observing.

00:04:17.361 --> 00:04:21.689
That if there is an I or Me observing
then I must not be what I am observing,

00:04:21.871 --> 00:04:24.729
then my internal must be
separate from my external.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.980
Watts would often refer to this as the sense
that we are an ego in a bag of skin.

00:04:29.207 --> 00:04:33.896
However in Zen in Watsons teachings this
concept and feeling is not only incorrect,

00:04:34.109 --> 00:04:39.450
but it is the source of most of our alienation
anxiety suffering and subsequent animosity.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:42.505
With the knowledge that we
will die that things will change

00:04:42.655 --> 00:04:46.214
that stuff will dissolve how can we derive
any sense of meaning or connection to life

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:49.713
by chaining our sense of self
to these things: to our body,

00:04:49.907 --> 00:04:52.897
to our personal identity,
to our stuff to our status.

00:04:53.104 --> 00:04:57.236
One of if not the most fundamental principle
in Zen and Watts's teachings

00:04:57.431 --> 00:04:59.674
is the idea that attempts
to resolve this problem.

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:03.148
The idea that we are none of these things
that we tend to identify with,

00:05:03.314 --> 00:05:06.210
but instead we are everything
and everything is us.

00:05:06.413 --> 00:05:11.337
Human and nature go together as one
linked inexorably in infinitely,

00:05:11.528 --> 00:05:15.759
just as noise can't exist without silence,
just as light can't exist without darkness,

00:05:15.954 --> 00:05:18.480
our internal cannot exist without our external

00:05:18.655 --> 00:05:22.934
and our experience cannot exist without
our non experience or death.

00:05:23.114 --> 00:05:26.275
Everything needs everything else
in order to be anything at all.

00:05:26.482 --> 00:05:29.507
Watts would often define this using
the term organism environment.

00:05:29.671 --> 00:05:33.513
Meaning we are not an organism in an
environment, but we are an organism

00:05:33.705 --> 00:05:35.891
and an environment simultaneously.

00:05:36.082 --> 00:05:40.195
We are but a feature of the whole
and thus we are the whole.

00:05:40.586 --> 00:05:44.342
For Watts the illusion that much of the
Western world has and continues to live in

00:05:44.552 --> 00:05:47.683
is that our thoughts are exempt
from the laws of the universe.

00:05:47.887 --> 00:05:50.508
That we have a separate volition
detached from nature

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.162
and our thoughts and actions occur
voluntarily and can impose themselves

00:05:54.362 --> 00:05:55.242
on nature.

00:05:55.452 --> 00:05:58.417
However for Watts the truth is
that our brain and our consciousness

00:05:58.617 --> 00:06:00.062
are not exempt or separate.

00:06:00.228 --> 00:06:02.474
Not from the cause and effect process
of the universe

00:06:02.643 --> 00:06:04.945
and not from the laws
that everything operates on.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:09.082
Within the Watson Zen school of thought
success in life is not to change the world

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.688
or to make a certain amount of wealth
or to surpass anyone and status or power

00:06:12.865 --> 00:06:16.173
or anything of that sort, but the
ultimate goal and success in life

00:06:16.378 --> 00:06:18.608
is to become deeply
synchronized with nature itself,

00:06:18.809 --> 00:06:22.394
to realize that your behaviour is one with
the behaviour of the rest of the world.

00:06:22.594 --> 00:06:24.394
A person is in fact nature itself

00:06:24.594 --> 00:06:27.515
and so a person cannot choose
to change or influence nature,

00:06:27.695 --> 00:06:30.287
because even what appears to
be a human effect on nature

00:06:30.476 --> 00:06:33.162
is only in essence
a nature effect on nature.

00:06:33.342 --> 00:06:36.352
Which is to say everything is just
nature playing the game of nature

00:06:36.552 --> 00:06:38.149
with us and through us.

00:06:38.335 --> 00:06:42.546
Like a river that flows without choosing
to or how to we humans move and act

00:06:42.776 --> 00:06:44.773
without choosing to or how to.

00:06:44.966 --> 00:06:47.595
We did not choose to be a human
or the kind of human we are.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:50.338
We did not choose the conditions
of the human body or mind.

00:06:50.544 --> 00:06:54.432
We simply express the nature of the universe
through them and the achievement of Zen

00:06:54.633 --> 00:06:57.812
is to flow freely without choosing,
acknowledging that one is

00:06:58.001 --> 00:06:59.869
and has always been without choosing.

00:07:00.048 --> 00:07:02.710
To accept this and overcome
one's ego is no small feat

00:07:02.924 --> 00:07:06.354
it is to destroy one sense of
self-importance which is of course

00:07:06.575 --> 00:07:10.479
very important to the thing that believes
and wants so very badly to be important.

00:07:10.658 --> 00:07:14.044
But the irony is that perhaps what we
think we want is not what we need.

00:07:14.264 --> 00:07:17.820
Perhaps thinking we are more or
less important than anything or anyone

00:07:18.002 --> 00:07:20.191
is not all that helpful for the
experience of life.

00:07:20.411 --> 00:07:24.185
Perhaps alternatively realizing one's
unimportance has the potential

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:28.990
to actually open up the door to a whole new
realm of meaningfulness and enjoyableness.

00:07:29.172 --> 00:07:33.435
Like an artist in a state of flow instead of
forcing nature we synchronize with it

00:07:33.646 --> 00:07:36.237
and perform life with fluidity and ease.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:40.487
Of course Watts is not without criticism
nor are the Eastern philosophies

00:07:40.665 --> 00:07:43.155
that he communicated and derived
many of his ideas from.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.703
It is reasonable to find some of Watt's
teachings and translations

00:07:46.892 --> 00:07:50.776
to be either confusing or fuzzy for ease up
against a very difficult opponent

00:07:50.965 --> 00:07:54.496
be it the very thing we have been
conditioned and wired to identify life with.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:58.489
Even for Watts himself it is fair to say
that the ideas he shared were not easy

00:07:58.647 --> 00:08:01.544
and did not resolve all the challenges
of being human for him.

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:05.611
According to those who knew him he was
not without struggle in her conflict or vice.

00:08:05.757 --> 00:08:09.492
Perhaps his take on life is accurate and
complete or perhaps it is not

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.537
and perhaps that is not the point.

00:08:11.707 --> 00:08:14.577
At this time in our evolution
we can only really speculate

00:08:14.757 --> 00:08:16.529
what the true nature of everything is.

00:08:16.709 --> 00:08:20.434
There is no answer at the back of the book
that we can peek at when things get confusing.

00:08:20.581 --> 00:08:21.782
However that does not mean that

00:08:21.943 --> 00:08:25.151
efforts and attempts at speculating and
understanding our spiritual essence

00:08:25.301 --> 00:08:26.221
is without value.

00:08:26.411 --> 00:08:30.755
Perhaps it is not the exact accuracy of
any philosophical idea that is important

00:08:30.899 --> 00:08:32.442
what the idea can do for us.

00:08:32.648 --> 00:08:37.342
For many Watts's ideas and offerings have and
continue to radically shift how they see

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:40.156
and experience life and a positive practical way,

00:08:40.326 --> 00:08:44.314
that Christianity and other traditional
Western ideologies continue to overlook.

00:08:44.494 --> 00:08:48.939
It is not only what Watts said but also
how he said it and who he said it to.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:52.026
In part Watt's fame can be
attributed to his unique ability

00:08:52.169 --> 00:08:55.345
to translate and communicate a way
out of the cycle of consumption,

00:08:55.505 --> 00:08:57.155
anxiety and alienation.

00:08:57.335 --> 00:09:01.528
In a part of the world that has and continues
to severely suffer from these things.

00:09:01.712 --> 00:09:03.131
For Watts and those who agree with him

00:09:03.291 --> 00:09:06.491
his teachings suggest very
comforting and useful ideas of life.

00:09:06.641 --> 00:09:10.565
That fundamentally there are
no mistakes, no failures, no successes,

00:09:10.698 --> 00:09:12.211
no good or bad things.

00:09:12.331 --> 00:09:16.011
Rather there are just things that happen,
that contrast with other things that happen.

00:09:16.198 --> 00:09:18.668
That life is not a contest
with winners and losers,

00:09:18.838 --> 00:09:20.581
but an endless game of back-and-forth.

00:09:20.731 --> 00:09:23.901
That we are not separate from everything,
but we are an expression of everything

00:09:24.071 --> 00:09:26.426
forever linked with
what has and will always be.

00:09:26.556 --> 00:09:28.903
And that we don't need to take
things quite so seriously.

00:09:29.032 --> 00:09:33.534
We're an ordinary person sees a battle,
an extraordinary person sees a cooperation,

00:09:33.674 --> 00:09:35.600
a dance as Watts would often call it.

00:09:35.724 --> 00:09:39.255
And there is no real point to a dance other
than to mystify and entertain.

00:09:39.421 --> 00:09:41.333
Which is to say everything and everyone

00:09:41.493 --> 00:09:44.783
is all working together at once
to mystify and entertain

00:09:44.943 --> 00:09:48.583
to express the single thing that is
universal consciousness that is life.

00:09:48.753 --> 00:09:51.688
And here we are in the stance with
an ability to form reason

00:09:51.838 --> 00:09:54.258
trying to make sense of this
apparently senseless dance.

00:09:54.428 --> 00:09:56.963
and our attempts we become
confused and seek better meaning,

00:09:57.109 --> 00:09:59.388
better justification,
better understanding.

00:09:59.537 --> 00:10:01.873
We overanalyse and take
ownership in this dance

00:10:02.033 --> 00:10:03.993
in order to compensate
for its elusiveness.

00:10:04.163 --> 00:10:05.784
We struggle to accept it for what it is.

00:10:05.954 --> 00:10:08.184
But perhaps there is
no better sense to anything,

00:10:08.364 --> 00:10:09.659
than senselessness.

00:10:09.814 --> 00:10:13.467
For in the senselessness there is wonder
mystification and entertainment.

00:10:13.639 --> 00:10:17.537
And perhaps it is this idea that remains
true no matter what we believe in life.

00:10:17.653 --> 00:10:20.420
Whether we agree with Watts,
Zen, Christianity

00:10:20.539 --> 00:10:23.140
or any of the other countless
religions and ideologies,

00:10:23.285 --> 00:10:26.636
we're almost certainly wrong
or incomplete in our understanding.

00:10:26.806 --> 00:10:29.376
And so for now perhaps the best we can do

00:10:29.546 --> 00:10:32.936
is to try and enjoy the dance
for what it is in all of its senselessness

00:10:33.059 --> 00:10:35.366
and remember that the only
thing that could be bad

00:10:35.475 --> 00:10:38.435
is to take it seriously.
- Alan Watts -

